<title>CAYMAN ISLANDS: Caribbean Electric to pay Class C dividend.</title>
<headline>Caribbean Electric to pay Class C dividend.</headline>
<dateline>GEORGETOWN, Cayman Islands 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caribbean Utilities Company, sole supplier of electrical power to this Caribbean British territory, announced it would pay a dividend of US$2 per fixed term Class C share on January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The dividend will be payable to Class C shareholders of record on January 17, 1997, a company statement said.</p>
<p>The 42 represents the quarterly dividend of the promised eight per cent on the shares, which are each worth $100.</p>
</text>
